Dear Ariel,
The bootstrapping procedure -- validate() -- described in Baayen's  
2008 book (6.2.4, pp. 193ff) typically consists of just 200 iterations  
on samples drawn with replacement from the original data set. This  
seems to be enough to determine the robustness of the model fit. You  
can specify the procedure for eliminating variables as well as the  
number of iterations.
Best,
John

